Subject: [PATCH] irqchip: vic: and pinctrl: exynos: make PM tracing opt-in

Upstream-Status: Pending

Normal suspend/resume and wake-mask programming are not diagnostic events.
Use dynamic-debug-compatible helpers instead of unconditional printk/debug
and info records. Error reporting and suspend behavior are unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-vic.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-vic.c
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-vic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-vic.c
@@ -105,1 +105,1 @@
-	printk(KERN_DEBUG "%s: resuming vic at %p\n", __func__, base);
+	pr_debug("%s: resuming vic at %p\n", __func__, base);
@@ -135,1 +135,1 @@
-	printk(KERN_DEBUG "%s: suspending vic at %p\n", __func__, base);
+	pr_debug("%s: suspending vic at %p\n", __func__, base);
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos.c b/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos.c
@@ -445,1 +445,1 @@
-	pr_info("wake %s for irq %u (%s-%lu)\n", on ? "enabled" : "disabled",
+	pr_debug("wake %s for irq %u (%s-%lu)\n", on ? "enabled" : "disabled",
